Each *.conf in this directory defines one harness. The filename is the harness
name: claude.conf is reached by `vaulted-agent claude`, or by the
claude-conductor symlink. `vaulted-agent pick` chooses from a menu.

`pick` is reserved: a harness named pick.conf shadows the chooser.

Recognised keys, all optional except command and manifest:

  backend  = onepassword | bitwarden | sops | pass | plainfile
             Defaults to DEFAULT_BACKEND in the launcher.
  manifest = the secrets to load. Relative names resolve under ../manifests/.
             This is the blast radius. Its format depends on the backend:
               onepassword  VAR=op://vault/item/field, resolved by `op inject`
               bitwarden    VAR=<secret-uuid>, one `bws secret get` each
               pass         VAR=store/entry/path, one `pass show` each
               sops         a sops-encrypted dotenv; the file IS the secrets
               plainfile    a plain dotenv; the file IS the secrets
  bin      = directory prepended to PATH before exec; $HOME expands
  workdir  = directory for the agent process before exec:
               (unset)  install WORKDIR (often the service account home)
               caller   the directory where you typed `va …` (best for
                        grok/claude --resume and project-scoped sessions)
               /path or $HOME/…  an explicit directory
  labels   = yes|no. Map non-UUID --resume/--session-id values to a UUIDv5.
             UUID-shaped --resume values are always passed through unchanged.
  keep     = extra environment variables surviving the scrub, comma separated.
  command  = the command line, split on whitespace
  arg      = one further argument, taken verbatim. Repeatable. Use this for
             any argument containing a space; `command` cannot express one.

  Extra CLI args after the harness name go to the agent, e.g.
    va grok --resume 019fabc1-…     |  va grok resume 019fabc1-…
    va claude --resume b03ca221-…   |  va claude resume b03ca221-…
    va codex resume 019fabc2-…      |  va codex --resume 019fabc2-…
  Shape is normalized per agent: codex wants `resume`; claude/grok want `--resume`.

Whitespace around the key, the `=`, and the value is ignored, so align them
however you like. Lines beginning with # are comments. The files are parsed,
never sourced: a value cannot execute shell.

Not harness keys. These are launcher-wide and live in ../defaults.conf, one
file for the machine rather than one per harness. Putting any of them here is
an error, because a harness must not choose them for itself:

  service_user    = the account harnesses run as; the launcher re-execs under
                    it via sudo. With this set, `workdir = caller` breaks
                    whenever you launch from a directory that account cannot
                    traverse -- a 0700 home being the usual case -- so prefer
                    an explicit workdir there.
  auth_mode       = file | prompt
  default_backend = backend for harnesses that omit `backend =`
  allow_run       = yes|no. `run` takes its command from the caller rather than
                    from a `command =` line, so it is refused by default once
                    service_user is set. Say yes to allow it deliberately.
